M55 E8 (PR14) -- is A.0.3's identity a measurement or algebra?
==============================================================================
   A.0.3 verifies FRC_i * P_i == Re(sum A conj B)/count to 1.4e-16.
   DERIVED: FRC_i = num/den and P_i = den/count, so the product is
   num/count for ANY complex A,B with den > 0.  The den cancels.  This
   is cancellation of a common factor, not a property of images.
   Testing whether ANY of the conventions the spec agonises over can
   break it.  If none can, the 1.4e-16 has no power (rule 21).

   case                        Re-form FRC*P vs canon   MAG-form FRC*P vs canon
   ordinary real, n=64              1.172e-16              2.000e+00   <-- MAG-form BREAKS
   ordinary real, n=64 +periodic Hann     0.000e+00              2.000e+00   <-- MAG-form BREAKS
   ordinary real, n=64 +ortho FFT     1.172e-16              2.000e+00   <-- MAG-form BREAKS
   ODD n=65                         0.000e+00              2.000e+00   <-- MAG-form BREAKS
   anti-correlated (neg)            0.000e+00              2.000e+00   <-- MAG-form BREAKS
   1e8 dynamic range                0.000e+00              0.000e+00
   COMPLEX-valued input             0.000e+00              2.682e+00   <-- MAG-form BREAKS
   identical a is b                 0.000e+00              0.000e+00

   The Re-form identity is exact under EVERY convention including odd n,
   complex input, ortho FFT and the wrong window.  It is algebra.
   The MAGNITUDE form of FRC -- the other standard convention, and the
   one m41lib's docstring describes -- BREAKS it wherever cross-power
   is negative.  That is an UNSTATED CONDITION on A.0.3.

